  "implementation": [
    "Step-up first validates the exact signed/correlated response, intrinsic user/task assurance and both current enrolled credentials under Binding authority. It does not pretend the successor is already the original native source.",
    "Successor dispatch, watch and authentication/assurance replies are prepared before physical media effects. The protected callback reuses the exact verified physical PeerAdmission/NativePhysicalBinding and the original observed Core credential rotation, preserving the original model and handles.",
    "The host releases initial/transition readers before fresh acquisition of current successor authority for the original blocked command. No larger reader is reacquired behind its own waiting writer. The private held intent retains its original envelope/body/logical operation/revision and executes once under the newly current command grant.",
    "A shared physical-transition marker and publication guard cover both auth.refresh and step-up. Cancellation/error after a possible transition, including a ready worker result not yet published, retires the physical root and children. A committed successor remains usable. The guard retains only its marker/token rather than bearer metadata.",
    "The explicit owned SDK APIs retain the one verified reader and only accept the exact correlated session/assurance transition. Definite authentication failure, application failure and unknown original execution remain distinct; no credential is issued or inherited."
  ],
